po"><addressbook><name>OSHIMURA MITSUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOMIZUKA KAZUMA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA HITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HANAOKA, KAZUNORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHIDA, ISAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUROIWA, YOSHIMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OSHIMURA, MITSUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOMIZUKA, KAZUMA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A cell having a modified foreign chromosome (fragment) is constructed by transferring the foreign chromosome into a cell having a high homologous recombination efficiency by the microcell fusion method, marking a desired site of the foreign chromosome by the homologous recombination method, and inducing deletion and/or translocation at the marked site. A method for constructing a nonhuman animal having a modified foreign chromosome (fragment) by using the above procedure; and a modified animal, a recombinant chromosome (fragment) and an artificial chromosomal vector each obtained thereby.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>On construit une cellule ayant un chromosome (fragment) étranger modifié, en transférant ce chromosome étranger dans une cellule possédant une efficacité de recombinaison homologue élevée par le procédé de fusion microcellulaire, en marquant un site souhaité de ce chromosome étranger par le procédé homologue, et en induisant une délétion et/ou une translocation au niveau du site ainsi marqué. Cette invention concerne également un procédé de synthèse d'un animal non humain, ayant un chromosome (fragment) étranger modifié, en utilisant le procédé présenté ci-dessus; ainsi qu'un animal modifié, un chromosome (fragment) recombiné et un vecteur chromosomique artificiel, qui sont chacun obtenus par le procédé présenté ci-dessus.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>